1.18.4: the encoder and the decoder were never on more than one core

The profile from 1.18.3 said it plainly: the pipeline stages scaled
five-fold on eight cores and save/load did not. pj_parallel_rows had a
"fewer than 64 rows is not worth a thread" cutoff written for pixel
rows; the JPEG encoder hands it 63 bands and the raw decoder 48 tiles,
so both ran serially on every machine. The cutoff is gone (the only
limit is one band per item), and the render's input copy is banded so
its pages are first touched in parallel. No arithmetic changed.
